  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.21851080"
    description: Version DOI for release v1.0.1
abstract: >-
  codehound is a zero-dependency static analyzer built on
  Python's standard-library ast module. It detects six
  classes of correctness and async-safety defect that recur
  in production Python AI/ML codebases: event-loop-blocking
  calls inside async functions, mutable default arguments,
  deprecated datetime.utcnow(), deprecated
  get_event_loop(), unclosed file handles, and
  fire-and-forget tasks eligible for garbage collection
  mid-run. Each rule is distilled from a defect found and
  fixed in a widely-used open-source AI/ML framework.
keywords:
  - static analysis
  - abstract syntax tree
  - Python
  - asyncio
  - concurrency defects
  - resource leaks
  - mining software repositories
  - empirical software engineering
